With Copilot cloud agent, you can let Copilot handle tasks in the background — from building new features to improving test coverage — while you focus actively on the work that really needs your attention.

You can get started by assigning an issue to Copilot or creating a task from the agents panel, available on every page on GitHub. <%= Copilot::COPILOT_SWE_AGENT %> is also integrated into Copilot Chat, Visual Studio Code, Microsoft Teams and a range of other tools.

When given a task, Copilot will:

- Immediately open a draft pull request and outline its plan
- Write code, and validate its changes with your automated tests and linter
- Request your review once it's done

As Copilot works, you can keep an eye on it with a new agent logs view that is integrated into the pull request.

To find out more about <%= Copilot::COPILOT_SWE_AGENT %>, head to the GitHub Docs: https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-docs

